Lobium — native screen / devicePixelRatio spoofing (JS-safe surface, done natively for coherence).

Reports the persona's screen geometry + DPR instead of the host display's, from the config channel's
already-parsed `screen.*` (width/height/availWidth/availHeight/colorDepth/devicePixelRatio). This closes
a real, easily-detected tell surfaced by the native detector run (ci/validation/lobium-detect.mjs):
every headless profile reported the default 800x600 (and, headful, the host monitor's true size),
contradicting the persona. Doing it natively (rather than via CDP setDeviceMetricsOverride, which mutates
the real viewport and has layout side effects) keeps rendering untouched — only the queried values change.

Three hook points (all reading LobiumFpConfig::Current(), all guarded on the config being present with a
positive screen width, else the real GetScreenInfo path runs unchanged):

  1. Screen::GetRect (core/frame/screen.cc) — the SINGLE shared source for
     width()/height()/availWidth()/availHeight()/availLeft()/availTop(), so one hook keeps all of them
     coherent. Returns the persona rect (CSS px): (0,0,width,height) for the full rect and
     (0,0,availWidth,availHeight) for the available rect. (Adversarial review confirmed this shared hook
     does NOT corrupt layout / media queries / fullscreen — only the JS-visible screen.* properties.)
  2. Screen::colorDepth (core/frame/screen.cc) — the persona colour depth; pixelDepth() delegates here.
  3. LocalDOMWindow::devicePixelRatio (core/frame/local_dom_window.cc) AND
     MediaValues::CalculateDevicePixelRatio (core/css/media_values.cc) — the persona DPR through BOTH the
     window.devicePixelRatio getter AND the CSS media-query resolution path, so
     matchMedia('(resolution: Xdppx)') / '(-webkit-device-pixel-ratio)' AGREE with the getter. Hooking
     the two disjoint DPR sources was required: an adversarial review found that overriding only the
     window getter left matchMedia reporting the REAL host DPR — a guaranteed, no-permission,
     trivially-scriptable lie for any persona whose DPR != host DPR (e.g. a 2x retina persona on a 1x
     host). The MediaValues-level hook keeps real raster/layout scale untouched.

The sidecar sizes the launch window to the AVAILABLE area (availWidth x availHeight — a maximized window),
not the full screen, so window.outerWidth/Height <= screen.avail* stays coherent (engine-runner
launch.ts; else outerHeight == screen.height > availHeight, an incoherence).

Proven on Chromium 152.0.7928.0 (SwiftShader, headless): baseline screen 800x600 -> persona
1920x1080 (Windows, dpr1) / 1512x982 (macOS, dpr2), availWidth/Height/colorDepth all match; DPR coherent
across window.devicePixelRatio AND matchMedia resolution + -webkit-device-pixel-ratio (macOS dpr2 on a
dpr1 host reports 2 everywhere); outerHeight <= availHeight. Detector gate: 9/9 surfaces, sannysoft 0-fail.

KNOWN LIMITATIONS (adversarial review — confirmed, deferred with rationale; see hooks.md):
  - macOS availTop is 0 (a real Mac's menu bar makes availTop ~25). Fixing it needs avail_left/avail_top
    threaded through shared-types + the catalog (derive.ts) so a Mac persona expresses a menu-bar inset;
    deferred as a cross-package follow-up. (Windows/Linux availTop=0 with a bottom taskbar is coherent.)
  - The Multi-Screen Window Placement API (getScreenDetails(): ScreenDetailed.devicePixelRatio/label,
    Screen.isExtended, getScreens() enumeration) still reflects real host values. These require the
    `window-management` permission prompt, so they are not silently scriptable — deferred.
  - Headful window outer-geometry is coupled to the persona only via the maximized-to-avail launch size;
    a native clamp of outerWidth/Height/screenX/Y to the persona rect (for when the host display exceeds
    the persona screen) is a follow-up.

Three hook points touch existing files (this patch); no added files, no BUILD.gn change (all in the
already-wired blink `core` component), no config change (screen.* already parsed by the config channel).
